            <ArticleTitle>[Three patients with the same diagnosis but very different symptoms].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>41-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1024/1661-8157/a001887</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present three cases of patients with a thoracic disc herniation with misinterpretation of the initial symptoms. In a first case, pulmonary symptoms were prominent; in a second case, the patient complained of cardiac symptoms; and in a third case, the patient reported neurological symptoms. Ineffective investigation of thoracic symptoms should raise the suspicion of a thoracic disc herniation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
